{
 "passion": {
  "title": "Follow Your Passion Is Bad Advice",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428031128/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=9dce9ebffa5d7b85eef1fa3ae9558f55cae7ead605282cd538d8afab9842a755",
  "beats": [
   "Follow your passion is bad advice.",
   "Most people can't name one.",
   "The advice excludes almost everyone.",
   "And in interviews, it shows.",
   "What do you want to do?",
   "You freeze. Nothing feels certain.",
   "Here's what is actually true.",
   "Passion isn't the start.",
   "It's the result of work.",
   "You get good at something.",
   "It starts giving something back.",
   "Then the feeling arrives.",
   "Interest comes first, not passion.",
   "Stop waiting to feel sure.",
   "Certainty is not the entry fee.",
   "Start from what holds attention.",
   "Not what excites you.",
   "What you lose time doing.",
   "Those are different feelings.",
   "Now use that in interviews.",
   "When they ask what you want,",
   "don't fake the certainty.",
   "Name the work, not the dream.",
   "More of this problem.",
   "Less of that other one.",
   "Specific, honest, and memorable.",
   "They hear passion all day.",
   "They can't tell it apart.",
   "Specific is what they remember.",
   "So write two lists tonight.",
   "Work that held your attention.",
   "Work that drained it.",
   "Apply toward the first list.",
   "You're not missing a passion.",
   "You haven't built one yet.",
   "Nobody starts out sure.",
   "Build it on interesting work.",
   "Interest comes first, every time."
  ]
 },
 "toolate": {
  "title": "It Is Not Too Late",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428033791/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=216838f8144ed4788837337afd161a1033dbe934ebec3b405fd794d0e47ce380",
  "beats": [
   "It is not too late.",
   "That is a belief, not a fact.",
   "It's the most expensive one",
   "a job seeker can carry.",
   "It doesn't stop you applying.",
   "It stops you applying properly.",
   "You apply, but half committed.",
   "You skip the roles you want.",
   "You apologise in line one.",
   "Sorry about the gap.",
   "Sorry about the career change.",
   "Nobody asked you to apologise.",
   "You volunteered it yourself.",
   "Here's what gets screened.",
   "Not age. Not a gap.",
   "Not a change of direction.",
   "What gets screened out is doubt.",
   "Confidence is the real filter.",
   "Unexplained gaps, not gaps.",
   "Vagueness, not the distance.",
   "An apology tells the reader",
   "there's a problem here.",
   "They had not seen one.",
   "Now they can see one.",
   "Replace the apology with facts.",
   "I took two years out.",
   "Here's what I did.",
   "Here's why I'm here now.",
   "Flat. Factual. No apology.",
   "That reads as control.",
   "Same with a career change.",
   "Not, I know this looks unusual.",
   "Instead, here's what carries over.",
   "People judge your timeline",
   "far less than you think.",
   "They judge whether you believe it.",
   "So lead with the reason,",
   "never with the apology."
  ]
 },
 "qualified": {
  "title": "Apply At Sixty Percent",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428034389/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=738811a338dadcc823fd0c0fe1c452f267ff4b9e5e02717ce6f8e46e4d14b5b5",
  "beats": [
   "Nobody is qualified for that job.",
   "Including whoever gets it.",
   "Look how postings get written.",
   "A manager lists their wants.",
   "Their team adds more.",
   "HR adds standard requirements.",
   "An old posting gets pasted in.",
   "Nobody ever removes anything.",
   "It becomes a wish list",
   "assembled by a committee,",
   "describing someone who doesn't exist.",
   "You read it as specification.",
   "No single person matches it.",
   "You count what you're missing.",
   "You find four. Tab closed.",
   "Someone with those gaps applied",
   "and is in second interviews.",
   "They didn't have more.",
   "They just didn't disqualify themselves.",
   "Here's a usable threshold.",
   "Sixty percent of the requirements.",
   "Meet that and you're inside",
   "the range they will consider.",
   "The rest was always negotiable.",
   "Gaps are expected, not fatal.",
   "Two things make this work.",
   "Be honest about the gap.",
   "Don't hide or bluff it.",
   "Name what sits beside it.",
   "I haven't used that tool.",
   "I've used the next one.",
   "That reads as confidence.",
   "Hiding reads as risk.",
   "Open the tab you closed.",
   "The one you doubted.",
   "Count again at sixty percent.",
   "Then apply to it anyway.",
   "That tab is still open."
  ]
 },
 "gauges": {
  "title": "You Might Not Need A New Job",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428034854/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=04a5e3b390e2abb5544414c7993dababcb0722972ce7f8ebc517279a8f874ef4",
  "beats": [
   "You might not need a new job.",
   "You might need a Saturday.",
   "Stay with me one second.",
   "Job searching exhausts you.",
   "It's rejection, on a schedule,",
   "from people who never reply.",
   "When you feel flat,",
   "your mind blames the obvious.",
   "The work. The market.",
   "Tiredness lies about its source.",
   "But there are four gauges.",
   "Health. Work. Play. Love.",
   "Rate each out of ten.",
   "Right now, honestly, this week.",
   "Most people find the same.",
   "Work is low. They knew.",
   "But play sits at zero,",
   "and they had not noticed.",
   "Every hour became search time.",
   "Weekends became guilt about applying.",
   "Everything enjoyable got postponed",
   "until the offer arrives.",
   "So the tank stays empty",
   "and the search gets blamed.",
   "Rest is part of searching.",
   "Here's why it matters.",
   "Empty people interview badly.",
   "They sound tired, because they are.",
   "They take the first offer,",
   "even when it's wrong.",
   "This week protect one thing.",
   "One evening that's not searching.",
   "Not a reward. A requirement.",
   "You're not being lazy.",
   "You're staying employable, deliberately.",
   "Burnt out people accept less.",
   "Refill the other gauges",
   "and you get harder to break."
  ]
 },
 "goodatit": {
  "title": "Being Good At It Is The Trap",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428035062/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=6aae7d48a8ce14da4150e5319427c959acb6c62b74cbec2d4f01e493142c104d",
  "beats": [
   "Being good at your job is the trap.",
   "Not the bad part.",
   "You got competent at something.",
   "People noticed. They gave more.",
   "You got better. More arrived.",
   "Now it's your whole resume.",
   "Your resume is a magnet.",
   "It pulls that role back.",
   "Recruiters see your last job.",
   "They offer more of it.",
   "Work you wanted to leave.",
   "This is how people stick",
   "in careers they never chose.",
   "Competence isn't a reason.",
   "Only a reason you can.",
   "Those are very different things.",
   "So ask yourself one question.",
   "If nobody praised this work,",
   "would you still do it?",
   "That separates skill from wanting.",
   "Praise is a poor compass.",
   "Now the practical part.",
   "You don't start over.",
   "Your skills transfer fine.",
   "Skills travel. Titles don't.",
   "The context is what changes.",
   "Same analysis, different industry.",
   "Same writing, different audience.",
   "Name the skill, not title.",
   "Then look for it elsewhere.",
   "Search by what you do,",
   "not what you were called.",
   "You'll find roles you missed",
   "because the title never matched.",
   "Good at work you dislike",
   "is a door, not a sentence.",
   "You chose once. Choose again."
  ]
 },
 "wrongproblem": {
  "title": "You Are Solving The Wrong Problem",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428035776/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=84751302e2e62cc2b7cd6c1fa1075412ff0a699328555bdc9f2b81a2b29a9dc6",
  "beats": [
   "You are solving the wrong problem.",
   "Solving it beautifully, too.",
   "Sixth resume version this month.",
   "New template. New summary line.",
   "Rewritten bullets. Tighter wording.",
   "And still nothing comes back.",
   "Here's the uncomfortable part.",
   "Effort isn't the missing piece.",
   "The document was never the problem.",
   "You're applying to the wrong roles.",
   "Too senior. Too generic.",
   "Wrong industry for your experience.",
   "No connection to anyone inside.",
   "A resume can't fix that.",
   "It's the right answer",
   "to a question nobody asked.",
   "Designers call this problem finding.",
   "It comes before problem solving.",
   "Most skip straight to solving,",
   "because solving feels productive.",
   "It's motion, not progress.",
   "Busy and stuck look identical.",
   "Try this before applying again.",
   "Open your last twenty applications.",
   "Look at the roles themselves.",
   "Not what you sent them.",
   "How many genuinely fit?",
   "How many had an insider?",
   "How many posted this week?",
   "That's your real diagnosis.",
   "If those answers are low,",
   "the resume was never it.",
   "Fix choosing, not writing.",
   "Ten well chosen applications",
   "beat two hundred written ones.",
   "Choosing is the real skill.",
   "Pick better, then write.",
   "Otherwise you polish forever."
  ]
 },
 "story": {
  "title": "Stop Asking For A Job",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428035733/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=54553a3ce51347a3520ded0541922047b7499af5cf49d0fe1dead03f94d27274",
  "beats": [
   "Stop asking people for jobs.",
   "Ask for their story instead.",
   "This sounds soft. It's not.",
   "Here's the actual mechanism.",
   "When you ask for work",
   "you hand someone a problem.",
   "They must say yes or no,",
   "and usually they have nothing.",
   "They avoid replying at all.",
   "You read that as rejection.",
   "It was discomfort, not rejection.",
   "Nobody owes you an opening.",
   "Now flip the ask completely.",
   "Ask how they got there.",
   "People like telling that story.",
   "It costs them nothing.",
   "There's no wrong answer.",
   "And almost nobody ever asks.",
   "Curiosity is easy to answer.",
   "So the reply rate changes.",
   "Same person. Same inbox.",
   "An entirely different question.",
   "Here's what to send.",
   "Two lines, not ten.",
   "One proving you looked.",
   "One asking how they got there.",
   "No resume. No attachment.",
   "No mention of any opening.",
   "Then when they reply, listen.",
   "Ask them one more thing.",
   "The opening surfaces by itself,",
   "or it doesn't. Fine either way.",
   "You never asked for it,",
   "you're not someone to refuse.",
   "You're someone they talked to.",
   "That's a different memory entirely.",
   "Send three this week.",
   "Reply rates change immediately."
  ]
 },
 "gravity": {
  "title": "Some Of Your Problems Are Gravity",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428036648/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=68a51dc561b190ea0138ab1dcd772bf651ed1a295888bf4e11bc1dabe8861a4e",
  "beats": [
   "Some problems are not problems.",
   "They're gravity, and gravity wins.",
   "The market is what it is.",
   "That role wants five years.",
   "You have three of them.",
   "Nobody is hiring in December.",
   "None of those are problems.",
   "They're conditions you stand on.",
   "A problem is something actionable.",
   "Here's why this matters.",
   "Conditions don't care about effort.",
   "You're spending real hours",
   "arguing with things that won't move.",
   "Rewriting a post nobody read.",
   "Refreshing a board that never updates.",
   "Rereading a rejection for reasons.",
   "That energy is gone.",
   "So make two columns tonight.",
   "Everything blocking your search.",
   "Left, things you can act on.",
   "Right, all of the rest.",
   "Be honest about the split.",
   "Then close the right column.",
   "Not solved. Simply accepted.",
   "Accepting isn't giving up.",
   "It's refusing to bleed energy.",
   "Work the left column only.",
   "This is not defeatism.",
   "Fewer applications, better chosen.",
   "One real conversation each week.",
   "One skills gap closed.",
   "Those things actually move.",
   "The market does not move.",
   "You have limited energy now.",
   "Spend it where it counts.",
   "Gravity was never your fault.",
   "Stop arguing with the weather.",
   "Fight only what moves."
  ]
 },
 "log": {
  "title": "A Two Week Log Beats Guessing",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428037163/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=38d39a63d99e28b2621cd1b9c6b0fe8d36b2e8198d16d1bc9184706765f52a08",
  "beats": [
   "Stop guessing which job to chase.",
   "Two weeks of notes answer it.",
   "Here's the whole method.",
   "Every day, write three lines.",
   "What you actually did.",
   "How engaged you were, roughly.",
   "How much energy it left.",
   "That's it. Three lines.",
   "Memory is a terrible witness.",
   "Do that for two weeks.",
   "Read it all at once.",
   "You're not looking for good days.",
   "You're looking for repeats.",
   "The same activity, high repeatedly.",
   "That's a real signal.",
   "The same one draining you twice",
   "is also a real signal.",
   "Now go one level deeper.",
   "For each high point, ask why.",
   "Was it the task itself?",
   "The people you were with?",
   "Solving, explaining, or organising?",
   "Those answers aren't job titles.",
   "Those are the real ingredients.",
   "Ingredients are what you search with.",
   "Most people search by title,",
   "and companies invent titles.",
   "They vary wildly between them.",
   "Ingredients don't vary like that.",
   "So shortlist from ingredients.",
   "Roles with many of your highs.",
   "Few of your drains.",
   "Then apply to those, narrowly.",
   "Patterns beat guessing at yourself.",
   "This isn't self discovery.",
   "It's data on yourself.",
   "Fourteen days and three lines",
   "beats another month of guessing."
  ]
 },
 "threelives": {
  "title": "You Have Three Next Jobs",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428037508/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=b7c33401818ca7f19f08dd6818568753eab3fc580e03025d52c62276518414a4",
  "beats": [
   "You don't have one next job.",
   "You have at least three.",
   "Writing them down changes everything.",
   "Here's the whole exercise.",
   "Three versions of your next role.",
   "All real. All different.",
   "Plan one is the obvious one.",
   "More of what you do now.",
   "The one your resume points at.",
   "Plan two is the backup.",
   "What if that field closed?",
   "Not a fantasy. A real one.",
   "The nearest thing you could reach.",
   "Plan three is the interesting one.",
   "If money were no issue",
   "and nobody was watching?",
   "Write all three. One page.",
   "Give each one a title.",
   "Here's why it works.",
   "One plan is one failure point.",
   "Rejection only devastates you",
   "when you have one plan.",
   "One plan makes every no fatal.",
   "Three plans make a no useful.",
   "That door closed. Two remain.",
   "This isn't positive thinking.",
   "It's structural. Weight spreads.",
   "There's a practical benefit.",
   "Plan three contains something real.",
   "A thread worth pulling.",
   "Some part is reachable now,",
   "usually a smaller version.",
   "So write the three tonight.",
   "Now check your applications.",
   "Most only serve plan one.",
   "Send some toward plan two.",
   "The search stops being a cliff.",
   "Three doors, not one."
  ]
 },
 "prototype": {
  "title": "Try The Job Before You Take It",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428038050/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=142bd717341f23e3cb29593bea2e296538981e7ac8874f57b65b08a8f137d9a0",
  "beats": [
   "You can try a career in a day.",
   "Most people commit years instead.",
   "Think how strange that is.",
   "You'd test drive a car.",
   "You'd try on a coat.",
   "A job you take blind,",
   "on a posting and two chats.",
   "You find out for real",
   "eighteen months in, wrong desk.",
   "Here's a better alternative.",
   "Certainty is cheaper than you think.",
   "Before committing, build a test.",
   "Not a change. A sample.",
   "Spend a day with someone.",
   "Ask to sit in quietly.",
   "Take one piece of work.",
   "A weekend project. A favour.",
   "One freelance job, badly paid.",
   "The point isn't money.",
   "The point is information.",
   "The test asks one question.",
   "Not, will I love this.",
   "Something answerable in a day.",
   "Do I like this problem?",
   "Can I stand this pace?",
   "Do these people energise me?",
   "That's a real result.",
   "A weekend is enough data.",
   "It costs one weekend.",
   "The alternative costs two years.",
   "Here's the part people miss.",
   "The test also builds contacts.",
   "You shadowed someone. They remember.",
   "You worked on something real.",
   "That's evidence, not claims.",
   "Pick the role you circle.",
   "Design one cheap test.",
   "Small tests beat big leaps."
  ]
 },
 "degree": {
  "title": "Your Degree Decided Nothing",
  "narration": "https://pikaso.cdnpk.net/private/production/5428038413/audio.mp3?token=exp=1789516800~hmac=791debe25b04803c22b252ee6f81598b30248cb3315906a8172ca120cf535046",
  "beats": [
   "Your degree decided nothing.",
   "Most people don't work",
   "in the field they studied.",
   "That's normal, not rare.",
   "But the belief is expensive.",
   "It keeps people in lane",
   "for years longer than needed.",
   "Here's how the trap works.",
   "Twenty year old you guessed.",
   "You chose one thing young.",
   "You built experience in it.",
   "Experience proves the degree right,",
   "and the degree justifies experience.",
   "It's a closed loop.",
   "Nobody outside that loop cares.",
   "Hiring people ask something simpler.",
   "Can this person do it?",
   "Your degree is one answer.",
   "It's not the only one.",
   "Here's the practical part.",
   "Changing field rarely means restarting,",
   "and rarely means school again.",
   "It means finding the overlap.",
   "Every field has a neighbour",
   "where your skill still works",
   "and the context is learnable.",
   "Not a leap. A step.",
   "Adjacent beats distant, every time.",
   "So find the bridge role.",
   "Find jobs naming your skill",
   "inside the industry you want.",
   "They exist. They're not",
   "advertised as career changes.",
   "Do that twice in three years",
   "and you've changed field entirely",
   "without a single new qualification.",
   "Your degree was a start.",
   "It was never an instruction.",
   "Sideways is still forward."
  ]
 }
}